  "result": "I found the cause of the `default_map` bug but haven't changed any code. Plan mode is on, and the tool for submitting the plan for approval isn't available in this session, so I'm stopping here.\n\n**Cause:** in `src/click/core.py` (lines 386\u2013392), a child `Context` inherits the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry for its own command name. With `{'runserver': {'port': 5000}}`, the subcommand looks for `port` at the top level of the map and never finds it.\n\n**Planned fix:** change line 392 from `default_map = parent.default_map` to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. I'd also add:\n- A `CHANGES.md` entry.\n- Tests in `tests/test_defaults.py` for a subcommand, a nested group, and a missing key falling back to the option default.\n\nThen I'd run the full `pytest`. The plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-swirling-bubble.md`.\n\nShould I go ahead and make these changes?",
